---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

---

<BaseLayout title="Private Training" description="Private soccer training in Morgan Hill, Gilroy, and Hollister with Sentinels coaches. One-on-one and small-group sessions for every level.">
<h1 class="vh">Private Soccer Training in Morgan Hill, Gilroy, and Hollister â€” Sentinels Soccer Club</h1>

    <section id="private-training" class="section">
        <div class="section-inner">
            <h2><span class="accent">Private</span> Training</h2>
            <div class="section-divider"></div>
            <p class="section-subtitle">
                One-on-one and small-group sessions designed around the individual player.
            </p>

            <!-- Hero intro -->
            <div class="pt-hero">
                <h2 style="margin-top:0">Personal Coaching. <span class="accent">Real Results.</span></h2>
                <p style="margin:0 auto;max-width:640px;font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.6">
                    Every player has a next step. Private training is how you get there faster â€”
                    focused reps, direct feedback, and a plan built around what your player needs most.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Original content pulled from Competitive page -->
            <p>
                One-on-one and small-group sessions are available with <strong>Coach Nolan</strong>,
                <strong>Coach Rick</strong>, and <strong>Coach Alex</strong>.
                <strong>Coach Nolan brings over 15 years of coaching experience</strong>. Private training focuses on
                individual skill development, position-specific work, and match preparation â€” the details
                that team practice does not always have time for.
            </p>

            <!-- Fresh content: Who it's for -->
            <h3>Who Private Training Is For</h3>
            <p>
                Private training works for players at every level. It is not just for the top competitive
                athletes â€” it is for any player who wants to grow. Common reasons families choose private
                sessions:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Newer players</strong> who need extra reps to build confidence with the ball.</li>
                <li><strong>Rec league players</strong> ready to level up before trying out for competitive.</li>
                <li><strong>Competitive team players</strong> who want to sharpen a specific weakness or position skill.</li>
                <li><strong>Goalkeepers</strong> looking for position-specific training you cannot get in a team session.</li>
                <li><strong>High school players</strong> preparing for tryouts, showcases, or the next season.</li>
                <li><strong>Returning players</strong> coming back from a break or an injury who need to rebuild rhythm.</li>
            </ul>

            <!-- What sessions cover -->
            <h3>What Sessions Cover</h3>
            <div class="pt-features">
                <div class="pt-feature">
                    <i class="fas fa-futbol"></i>
                    <h4>Ball Mastery</h4>
                    <p>First touch, close control, and confidence with both feet under pressure.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pt-feature">
                    <i class="fas fa-bullseye"></i>
                    <h4>Shooting &amp; Finishing</h4>
                    <p>Technique, placement, and decision-making in the final third.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pt-feature">
                    <i class="fas fa-arrows-alt"></i>
                    <h4>Passing &amp; Vision</h4>
                    <p>Weight of pass, timing, and scanning the field before you receive.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pt-feature">
                    <i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i>
                    <h4>Defending</h4>
                    <p>Positioning, body shape, and reading the game to win the ball back.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pt-feature">
                    <i class="fas fa-hands"></i>
                    <h4>Goalkeeper Training</h4>
                    <p>Distribution, footwork, positioning, and shot-stopping fundamentals.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pt-feature">
                    <i class="fas fa-brain"></i>
                    <h4>Game Awareness</h4>
                    <p>Reading play, tactical decisions, and playing your position at a higher level.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pt-feature">
                    <i class="fas fa-heartbeat"></i>
                    <h4>Fitness &amp; Speed</h4>
                    <p>Sport-specific conditioning that translates directly to match performance.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="pt-feature">
                    <i class="fas fa-calendar-check"></i>
                    <h4>Tryout Prep</h4>
                    <p>Targeted sessions leading up to competitive tryouts or high school selections.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- How it works -->
            <h3>How It Works</h3>
            <div class="comp-split">
                <div class="comp-card">
                    <h3><i class="fas fa-user"></i> One-on-One Sessions</h3>
                    <p>
                        A single player and a coach. Fully personalized to that player's goals, weaknesses,
                        and current level. This is the fastest way to see focused improvement.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Sessions are typically 45 to 60 minutes and can be scheduled weekly, biweekly, or in
                        block series leading up to a specific goal (tryouts, showcase, high school season).
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="comp-card">
                    <h3><i class="fas fa-user-friends"></i> Small-Group Sessions</h3>
                    <p>
                        Two to four players training together. Great for teammates who want to grow together,
                        siblings, or friends at a similar skill level. Adds competitive reps and game-realistic
                        pressure while keeping the coaching personal.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Small-group sessions are more affordable per player and often produce faster tactical
                        growth thanks to the live opponent element.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Coaches highlight -->
            <div class="philosophy-box" style="margin-top:32px">
                <h3><i class="fas fa-user-tie" style="color:var(--green,#4a7c00)"></i> Your Private Training Coaches</h3>
                <p>
                    <strong>Coach Rick, Coach Nolan, and Coach Alex</strong> lead our private training program.
                    All three bring years of coaching experience â€” Nolan and Alex are former collegiate athletes
                    and college graduates, and Rick serves as our Director of Coaching and Technical Director.
                    Every private session is led by a coach who understands how to develop players, not just
                    run drills.
                </p>
                <p style="margin-bottom:0">
                    <a href="/coaches"><strong>Meet the full coaching staff â†’</strong></a>
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- CTA -->
            <div class="pt-cta">
                <h3 style="margin-top:0">Ready to Book a Session?</h3>
                <p>
                    Reach out and let us know your player's age, current level, and what you want to work on.
                    We will match you with the right coach and get you on the schedule.
                </p>
                <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">
                    <i class="fas fa-envelope"></i> Inquire About Private Training
                </a>
                <p style="margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:0">
                    Or reach us directly at
                    <a href="mailto:sentinelssoccerclub@gmail.com"><strong>sentinelssoccerclub@gmail.com</strong></a>
                    or <strong>(408) 722-1028</strong>.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>